lysis from acetaldehyde\",\n      \"description\": \"The acetaldehyde Strecker product is first hydrolyzed only to alaninamide, then to DL-alanine before L-selection.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_003\", \"rxn_005\", \"rxn_006\", \"rxn_012\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_008\", \"mol_009\", \"mol_013\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P3\",\n      \"name\": \"Hydantoin route from acetaldehyde\",\n      \"description\": \"Acetaldehyde is trapped as 5-methylhydantoin under cyanide, ammonia, and carbonate conditions, then hydrolyzed to alanine and resolved.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_007\", \"rxn_008\", \"rxn_012\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_010\", \"mol_013\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"name\": \"Cyanohydrin to pyruvate from acetaldehyde\",\n      \"description\": \"Acetaldehyde first forms lactonitrile, which is converted to pyruvate and then reductively aminated to alanine before L-enrichment.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_009\", \"rxn_010\", \"rxn_011\", \"rxn_012\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_011\", \"mol_012\", \"mol_013\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n      \"name\": \"Direct pyruvate entry\",\n      \"description\": \"An independently generated pyruvate pool feeds directly into hydrothermal reductive amination and subsequent L-selection.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_011\", \"rxn_012\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_012\", \"mol_013\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n      \"name\": \"Formaldehyde-derived acetaldehyde to direct Strecker\",\n      \"description\": \"Formaldehyde dimerizes to glycolaldehyde, is reduced to acetaldehyde, and then follows the direct Strecker-hydrolysis branch.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_012\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_006\", \"mol_007\", \"mol_008\", \"mol_013\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P7\"